From e8bd8bcc6aa5d8436e059f8b6a8d4fe4bb333423 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomtomnet <tompere8000@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:00:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/24] ui, virtio-gpu: zero copy with held flush fences and
 host deadlines; the ImGui menu dropped

- virtio-gpu: a flush fence of context 0 can be held until the compositor releases the
  previous buffer (zero copy: the guest must not render into a buffer still on the screen);
  the host compositor's latching deadline as a vblank target (x-vblank-deadline,
  x-vblank-deadline-margin, x-vblank-swap-target-zc); traces;
- console: the swap and deadline times through graphic_hw_gl_flushed();
- D-Bus display: zero copy of the guest's scanout buffers and the client's presentation
  feedback (dbus-display1.xml, listener, console);
- SDL window: its own swapchain's zero copy path and stats (x-query-display-stats fields
  zero-copy, host-scanout);
- the in-window ImGui control menu removed (removed from the fork 2026-10-08) with its
  subproject, build option and the NIC byte counter it showed.

Split out of the 2026-10-12 snapshot of the fork's uncommitted work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
